// Read-only lookups are always allowed, including both approval lookups.
// The approval lookups need their own permit, otherwise they are recorded
// as errors and could never serve as evidence for a close.
@id("allow-readonly-lookups")
permit (principal, action in [
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes",
    Drupe::Action::"Tolvick___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"Wexlow___get_tolvick_approval"
], resource);

// Close at MAIN, backed by a recent completed Tolvick lookup that confirmed
// an ACCEPTED decision by a PERSON for this exact work order and site.
@id("close-with-person-approval-tolvick")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Tolvick___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};

// Same rule, with the approval confirmed through the Wexlow lookup of the Tolvick approval.
@id("close-with-person-approval-wexlow")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Wexlow___get_tolvick_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED",
    output.approver_kind: Drupe::approver_kind::"PERSON"
  }
};

// The agent may never approve work orders, whatever else is permitted.
@id("forbid-agent-approval")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___approve_workorder", resource);
```

Everything not listed is denied by default: assign, cancel, update, generate, and closes at any other site.

I accepted the Wexlow lookup as approval evidence because it returns the same Tolvick approval data. If Wexlow should only be a read-only lookup, delete the `close-with-person-approval-wexlow` policy; the lookup stays permitted.

I wrote the `decision` and `approver_kind` matches as enum entity literals, e.g. `Drupe::decision::"ACCEPTED"`, because the schema declares those fields as enum entities. The authoring reference only shows string literals for output fields, so I haven't confirmed this form validates.

